{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-4","title":"Santiago 1:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Introducción al libro - Santiago Lea el primer capítulo de Santiago ESCRITOR: Santiago (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 4:21&quot;), llamado &quot;el Justo&quot; mencionado por Pablo con Cefas y Juan como &quot;columnas&quot; en la iglesia de Jerusalén Gálatas 2:9. Parece haber sido, como hombre religioso, austero, legal, ceremonial Hechos 21:18-24. FECHA: La tradición fija el martirio de Santiago en el año 62, pero su Epístola no muestra rastros de las revelaciones más amplias acerca de la iglesia y las doctrinas distintivas de la gracia hechas a través del apóstol Pablo, ni siquiera de la discusión acerca de la relación de los gentiles conversos con la ley de Moisés, que culminó en el primer concilio (Hechos 15), que presidió Santiago. Esto supone la fecha muy temprana de Santiago, que con confianza puede establecerse como &quot;la primera Epístola a los cristianos&quot;. -Weston. TEMA: Por &quot;las doce tribus dispersas&quot; debemos entender, no a los judíos, sino a los judíos cristianos de la dispersión. La iglesia comenzó con Hechos 2:5-11 y Santiago, que parece no haber abandonado Jerusalén, sentiría una responsabilidad pastoral particular por estas ovejas dispersas. Todavía recurrían a las sinagogas, o llamaban a sus propias asambleas con ese nombre (Santiago 2:2, donde &quot;asamblea&quot; es &quot;sinagoga&quot; en gr.). De Santiago 2:1-8 se desprende que todavía tenían los tribunales de la sinagoga para juzgar las causas que surgían entre ellos. La Epístola, entonces, es elemental en extremo. Suponer que Santiago 2:14-26 es una polémica contra la doctrina de la justificación de Pablo es absurdo. Ni Gálatas ni Romanos se escribieron todavía. El tema de Santiago, entonces, es la &quot;religión&quot; (del griego threskeia, &quot;servicio religioso externo&quot;) como expresión y prueba de la fe. No exalta las obras en contra de la fe, sino la fe como productora de obras. Su estilo es el de los libros de Sabiduría del A.T. Las divisiones son cinco: La prueba de la fe 1:1-2:26 La realidad de la fe probada por la lengua, 3:1-18 La reprensión de la mundanalidad, 4:1-17 Los ricos advertidos 5 Exhortatorio perfecto, maduro y completo. (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 5:48&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-14","title":"Santiago 1:14","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>tentado &quot;Tentación&quot; se usa en dos sentidos: (1) Solicitud al mal (por ejemplo, Génesis 3:1-6; Mateo 4:1; 1 Corintios 10:13; 2 Corintios 11:3,4; Santiago 1:14). (2) Prueba bajo juicio (por ejemplo) Génesis 22:1; Lucas 22:28 Cf Lucas 4:2, Cf Mateo 6:13 (solicitud al mal) y 1 Pedro 1:6 (prueba bajo juicio).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-14","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-15","title":"Santiago 1:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>pecado Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-17","title":"Santiago 1:17","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>regalo En el original se utilizan dos palabras para &quot;regalo&quot;, la primera significa el acto de dar; el segundo, la cosa dada.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-17","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-20","title":"Santiago 1:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>justicia (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:21&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-20","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-21","title":"Santiago 1:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>guardar (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 1:16&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-21","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-26","title":"Santiago 1:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>religioso (griego - θρη̑σκος = aparentemente religioso).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-26","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-1-27","title":"Santiago 1:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>mundo &quot;kosmos&quot; = sistema-mundo. Santiago 4:4; Juan 7:7 (véase Scofield &quot;Apocalipsis 13:8&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-1-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-1","title":"Santiago 2:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>el Señor de la gloria, la Gloria, es decir, en el sentido de Hebreos 1:3 como tomando el lugar de la shekinah. con respeto En presencia de Cristo la Gloria, las distinciones terrenas desaparecen.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-5","title":"Santiago 2:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>mundo kosmos = humanidad. (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 4:8&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-9","title":"Santiago 2:9","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>pecado Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-9","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-11","title":"Santiago 2:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>pecado transgresor. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-11","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-14","title":"Santiago 2:14","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>guardar (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 1:16&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-14","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-21","title":"Santiago 2:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>justificado (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 4:2&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-21","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-22","title":"Santiago 2:22","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>perfecto (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 5:48&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-22","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-2-23","title":"Santiago 2:23","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>imputación La imputación es el acto de Dios por el cual Él atribuye justicia al creyente en Cristo, quien ha llevado los pecados del creyente en vindicación de la ley. (véase Scofield &quot;Filemón 1:18&quot;). justicia (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:21&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-2-23","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-3-1","title":"Santiago 3:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>domina a los maestros, sabiendo que tendremos el juicio más severo. cf. Marcos 12:40.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-3-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-3-2","title":"Santiago 3:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>perfecto (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 5:48&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-3-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-3-6","title":"Santiago 3:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>infierno (véase Scofield &quot;Mateo 5:22&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-3-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-3-18","title":"Santiago 3:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>justicia (véase Scofield &quot;1 Juan 3:7&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-3-18","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-4-4","title":"Santiago 4:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>mundo &quot;kosmos&quot; = sistema-mundo. 2 Pedro 1:4; Juan 7:7 (véase Scofield &quot;Apocalipsis 13:8&quot;)</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-4-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-4-6","title":"Santiago 4:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>gracia Gracia (impartida). 1 Pedro 2:19; Romanos 6:1; 2 Pedro 3:18</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-4-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-4-8","title":"Santiago 4:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>pecadores Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-4-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-4-12","title":"Santiago 4:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>guardar (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 1:16&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-4-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-4-17","title":"Santiago 4:17","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>pecado Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-4-17","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-5-1","title":"Santiago 5:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>pecado Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-5-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-5-4","title":"Santiago 5:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>el Señor de los ejércitos, es decir, Jehová de los ejércitos.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-5-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-5-16","title":"Santiago 5:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>faltas Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;). justo (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 10:10&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-5-16","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-jas-5-20","title":"Santiago 5:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>pecados Pecado. (véase Scofield &quot;Romanos 3:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-jas-5-20","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}}]}
